course: dictionary
lesson: 7968
title: Saying it from memory
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To recite something is to say it aloud from memory, without reading it from a page. «The Gryphon orders her to stand up and recite «'Tis the voice of the sluggard».» The words stand up and recite show the child is speaking out loud in front of others, and she has to know the poem by heart.
explain: Look for clues that tell you about memory. In Victorian schools, children learned poems by heart and recited them standing up. «How doth the little busy bee» is a poem Alice gets wrong, so she is trying to remember it and failing. Her mistakes are the clue that recite means to say from memory.
explain: Recite can also mean saying a list of things one after another. «Recite the alphabet» or «recite your times tables» means say them in order, without looking anything up. In a phone call, you might recite your phone number, and in a long complaint, a person might recite every problem they have had.
fact: Recite means to say something aloud from memory.
fact: Recite is a verb: I recite, he recites, we recited, we are reciting.
fact: To recite a list is to say many things one after another, like names, facts or numbers.
fact: Victorian children often learned poems by heart and recited them standing up.
fact: Muslims believe the Qur'an is God's word, and it is recited in Arabic.
exercise: «The Gryphon orders her to stand up and recite «'Tis the voice of the sluggard».» What does recite mean here? | To sing a poem to a tune | To write a poem down on paper | *To say a poem aloud from memory | To read a poem silently from a book
exercise: In «giggled shyly … and remained absolutely tongue-tied», which word means unable to speak because of nerves? | absolutely | *tongue-tied | shyly | giggled
exercise: Mum says, «Recite your times tables for me.» What is she asking you to do? | To buy a new book of times tables | To draw a picture of the times tables | *To say the times tables aloud from memory | To write the times tables in a notebook
test: Teacher says, «Recite the alphabet.» What does she want? | To spell out a word you cannot read | To count how many letters there are in a sentence | *To say the letters in order from memory | To paint the letters on the wall
test: Which action is reciting? | Writing a poem on a card | Drawing a picture of a poem | Reading a poem from a book out loud | *Saying a poem aloud with no book, from memory
exam: In «The Mole asks one of them to recite from last year's play», what does recite mean? | To read the play silently in the library | To write a new play for next year | *To say the lines aloud from memory | To paint the scenery for the play
